(a) There are infinitely many super special positive integers;
(b) The integer 2014 is not super special.

Determine all fourth-degree polynomials $p(x)$ satisfying the following:
(1) $p(x)$ is even, i.e., $p(x) = p(-x)$ for all $x$;
(2) $p(x) \geq 0$ for all real $x$;
(3) $p(0) = 1$;
(4) $p(x)$ has precisely two local minima at points $x_1$ and $x_2$ with $|x_1 - x_2| = 2$.

Consider a complete graph $K_n$ with $n \geqslant 3$ vertices, where each vertex represents a cave and each edge represents a unique path between two caves. A campaign is defined as a Hamiltonian cycle in the graph, starting and ending at the same vertex, visiting all other vertices exactly once, and traversing edges without repetition. Furthermore, no edge is used in more than one campaign.

a) Show that for any prime $n$, the maximum number of such disjoint Hamiltonian cycles is $\frac{n-1}{2}$;

b) Determine the maximum number of disjoint Hamiltonian cycles for $n = 9$.

An $n \times n$ grid contains one beetle in each cell. At a given moment, each beetle simultaneously moves to a neighboring cell (two cells are neighboring if they share a side). Determine the maximum number of cells that can be left empty after the beetles have moved, for

a) $n = 8$;

b) $n = 9$.

